%S A399822 1,1,1,1,4,38,1148,75166,10382344,3150051632,1991252642288,
%T A399822 2576052178978936,6725883292958350024
%N A399822 Number of labeled neighborhood-Sperner graphs on n vertices.
%C A399822 A graph is neighborhood-Sperner if the family of its open neighborhoods {N(v) : v in V(G)} is a Sperner family; equivalently, N(u) is not a subset of N(v) for any two distinct vertices u and v.
%H A399822 L. H. Clark, S. Holliday, J. P. McSorley and T. D. Porter, <a href="https://opensiuc.lib.siu.edu/math_articles/119/">Enumerating labelled graphs with certain neighborhood properties</a>, Congressus Numerantium 190 (2008), 193-206.
%e A399822 a(4) = 4: the neighborhood-Sperner graphs on 4 labeled vertices consist of K_4 and the three labeled copies of 2K_2.
%Y A399822 Cf. A399817 (labeled neighborhood-Hausdorff graphs).
